{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T2-001", "approach": "B1", "approach_base": "B1", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "**Answer:**  \nThe virtue he found hardest to acquire was **#3 Order**.  \n\n**Reasons for the difficulty**  \n1. **Occupation constraints** – As a journeyman printer, his work “mix[ed] with the world, and often receive[s] people of business at their own hours” (Evidence [3]).  \n2. **Time pressure** – He noted that the scheme of Order “might be practicable where a man's business was such as to leave him the disposition of his time” (Evidence [2]).  \n3. **Lack of habit** – He had “not been early accustomed to it” and, despite an “exceeding good memory,” he was “not so sensible of the inconvenience attending want of method” (Evidence [3]).  \n4. **Frequent relapses** – The article “cost me so much painful attention… and had such frequent relapses” that he almost gave up the attempt (Evidence [3]).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 9 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::o031", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::p1_b376"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 0, "span": [187016, 187025], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 84 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::o031", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::p1_b377"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 1, "span": [187027, 187111], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 2225 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::o031", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::p1_b422"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 2, "span": [195322, 197547], "meta": {}}], "evidence_units": ["